-- statement:
--   Exact certificate data (part 2 of 2) for Case 1 ($t_{ij}\ge-\tfrac9{10}$ for all pairs) in H. Tran's proof of the Thomson problem for seven electrons. Together the two parts contain the untyped three-point certificate of Case 1 (paper §5.2): the PSD blocks $F_0,\dots,F_3$, the minorant coefficients $h_0,\dots,h_{10}$, the constant $e$ and the sum-of-squares Gram blocks $S_0,\dots,S_7$, all as integers over the common denominator $2^{160}$.
--
--   These are plain data definitions (integers, integer polynomials and block encodings); their correctness is not assumed anywhere — the solution of the corresponding cell lemma checks every identity and positivity condition in the Lean kernel. The data are split into two files only to respect the platform's file-size limit, and this part imports part 1.
--
--   **Formalization Note** The code is taken verbatim from the source file, restricted to the declarations needed here; the only edits for this Lean/Mathlib version are the lemma renames `ite_eq_left`→`if_pos`, `ite_eq_right`→`if_neg` and one rewrite of `IsHermitian.isSymm`.
